@madbrain76 add this:

"my-local": {
  "npm": "@ai-sdk/anthropic" // <<< THIS
}

Then tell me if it makes a difference

Your provider isn't configured correctly, this looks like a custom provider:
```
"provider": {
    "my-provider": {
      "api": "<SOME API>",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "models": {
        "gpt-5.5": {
          "provider": {
            "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai",
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
```

Do something like this, if you designate the openai sdk it will use responses, if you use openai-compatible it will use completions

You can define it at the provider and override it per model if you want (not necessary to define per model unless ur overriding)

Made a PR, for now you can do this:
```
"provider": {
    "google-vertex-anthropic": {
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4-6": {
          "options": {
            "toolStreaming": false,
          },
        },
    },
  },
```

You can pass that option for each model u wanna disable it for

